text:
ana: CI linkcheck failed on the docs site — lots of 404s for intra-doc anchors. Root cause seems headings that include inline code (backticks). Example from the built HTML: <h2 id="how-to-call-the-`embed()`-helper">... which obviously breaks links.

rocks: docs-bot: linkcheck job #157 failed in workflow docs/build — 12 broken anchors (see CI artifacts: https://ci.redwood.ai/artifacts/docs/linkcheck/157).

mike: ah yeah — the MDX slugger is being a bit too literal. The generated id ends up with backticks (something like how-to-call-the-`embed()`-helper). Browsers/links don't normalize that, so links like #how-to-call-the-embed-helper don't match.

jia: quick options: 1) edit the heading and add an explicit plain id (e.g. add an <a id="how-to-call-the-embed-helper"></a> or use an inline id), 2) add a small remark plugin that normalizes slugs (strip code ticks and other punctuation), or 3) update the link targets to match the slugger output (ugly but fast).

sam: I can prototype a small fixer that scans the built HTML and reports mismatched anchors — will make bulk fixes safer.

mike: for the immediate page causing most traffic (sdk/snippets) I'll add an explicit anchor to unblock users, then we can land a general fix.

ana: can we also catch this in lint/CI so future PRs fail earlier? linkcheck catches it but it's a slower loop. A pre-merge lint that flags headings with inline code would be ideal.

sam: opening a PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4321 — draft includes a remark-plugin that strips backticks from generated ids and a docs-lint rule that flags headings containing inline code. Also added a small unit test.

mike: nice. I opened a tiny companion PR that updates the few affected pages with explicit ids and fixes the immediate links: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4322. That should make the deploy preview usable.

ana: thanks — please add a brief note in the PR description explaining tradeoffs (explicit id vs plugin) so reviewers understand the choice. Also add a changelog entry under docs/migrations.md.

sam: done — added the explanation and a migration note. Also added a check that the plugin runs during local build so contributors get the same slugs locally.

docs-bot: deploy preview created — https://deploy-preview-4321--docs.redwood.ai (linkcheck running on preview).

ana: I'll wait for the preview linkcheck to pass, then merge both PRs in order (4322 first, then 4321). If the preview still shows broken anchors we'll rollback 4322 and iterate.

mike: FYI reproduction steps for anyone who wants to test locally: run `yarn workspace docs build && yarn workspace docs run linkcheck` or use `./scripts/docs-linkcheck.sh` which mimics CI.

jia: leaving a tiny example of a remark plugin (simplified) that normalizes heading ids in case it's useful to copy into the PR:

```
// remark plugin (simplified)
const visit = require('unist-util-visit');
module.exports = function stripCodeTicks() {
  return (tree) => {
    visit(tree, 'heading', (node) => {
      if (node.data && node.data.hProperties && node.data.hProperties.id) {
        node.data.hProperties.id = node.data.hProperties.id.replace(/[`']/g, '');
      }
    });
  };
};
```

ana: Great catch everyone. I'll add a short note in the migration guide so authors know: avoid inline code in headings or add explicit ids.

mike: :tada:
